A||N||4||Rogue_Ant||Ran poorly, then died.||||9||
Z||000000||Rogue_Ant||09-06-2001||03:59 PM||||First I have an 85GT Auto.<BR>Ok, I just got done taking out my water seperator, putting on new exaust manifolds, that I ported.  It has new plugs, wires, distributer, coil, and K&N air filter.  Then I pulled off the vaccume to the Fuel Vapor Canister and the vaccume to the EGR valve;  also I put breathers in place of the PVC system.  I blocked off the vaccumes that weren't being used anymore and I also pulled off the Cruise, and no muffler, just cat.  I set base timming at 8 degrees and started it up.  It backfired real bad, continueously.  I drove it for a little while and it stopped backfiring 'cept for around 1100rpm.<BR>Now the problem is the car feels like it has ~70hp and moving the distributer doesn't really effect it.  I bumped the timming up to 12 degrees and drove around with no noticable change in power.  That is when I just died.  It stalled and now I can't get it started.  It has spark, air, I need to get my pressure gauge and check fuel pressure.  But I'm kinda stummped.<BR>Does anyone know why pulling off the emmisions BS would do this?<BR>oh and I don't have to worry about emmisions since my car is registered in Iowa.<P>Rogue||||reg||9
Z||000001||Fierowrecker||09-06-2001||06:19 PM||||Hey Rogue!<BR>Sounds like crossed plug wires...<BR>But that is just a guess...<BR>crash...<P>------------------<BR>crash... The Fierowrecker<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://fiero.nl/uploads/crash_sig.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||87GTZ34||09-06-2001||06:25 PM||||Make sure you didn't disconnect the MAP sensor.  Although I don't think disconnecting it would make it go that sour.  My suggestion would be to put a vacuum gauge on it and that will tell you if you have any vacuum leaks and more importantly tell you if the cam timing has jumped, or it can't get a good breath to make decent vacuum.  Also the backfiring and hickup-ing is a sign of a lean condition.  can you get a scanner to take the computer readings?||||reg||1
Z||000003||Rogue_Ant||09-08-2001||07:02 PM||||Fierowrecker:<BR>Hmm, I will check but the engine did sound smooth enough after it stopped its relentless backfiring.<P>87GTZ34:<BR>I will get a vacuum Gauge on it as soon as I can, which will prob be around the 16th.  A scanner will be harder to come accross as I would have to buy it.  I did check the MAP sensor and it is connecet.  One interesting thing is when it died on the road I checked for fuel - I unscrewed the cap on the rail, and pressed the little button in with my finger, and nothing came out.  As far as I know fuel should've been ~45psi (prob less since the car wasn't running).  So we cranked it over, and some fuel cam out, but just dribbled.<BR>Any comments about pulling off the emissions stuff?<P>Rogue<p>[This message has been edited by Rogue_Ant (edited 09-08-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||87GTZ34||09-08-2001||09:06 PM||||No that wouldn't make it run badly.  Right now, I have my vapor canister and egr solenoid bypassed (until I can buy new ones)as they are both shot and leaking vacuum.  Running w/o the EGR may cause slight pinging under moderate acceleration.  You probably nailed your problem with the fuel supply.  See if auto stores in your area loan or rent tools cheap and see if they have the vac gauge and  fuel pressure gauge.  If you haven't replaced the fuel filter already, you may want to try that as these cars are pretty old and usually not maintained very well.  GL<BR>Anybody in the Col Spings/Ft Carson area have an autoXray or other scanner to help out Rogue?<P>Edited for typos<p>[This message has been edited by 87GTZ34 (edited 09-08-2001).]||||reg||1
